{
  "category": "Larva Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Its strong jaw enables it to scrape trees and slurp out the sap. It normally lives underground.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "They often gather near places frequented by electric Pokémon in order to avoid being attacked by bird Pokémon.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "If you find its nest, you shouldn’t stick your hand inside. You’ll get bitten by an irritated Grubbin.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It spits a sticky thread to stop opponents in their tracks, and then it grabs them in its sharp, sturdy mandibles to take them down.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its natural enemies, like Rookidee, may flee rather than risk getting caught in its large mandibles that can snap thick tree branches.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "It uses its big jaws to dig nests into the forest floor, and it loves to feed on sweet tree sap.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
